Package: exposomeSC
Title: Cell-Type-Resolved Exposome-Wide Association Studies for
    Single-Cell RNA-seq
Version: 0.99.2
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Cuiwei",
           family = "Gao",
           email = "48gaocuiwei@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tests donor-level environmental exposures for
    association with gene expression within cell types in single-cell
    RNA-seq cohorts (single-cell exposome-wide association studies,
    sc-ExWAS). The package extends SingleCellExperiment to hold
    donor-level exposure measurements alongside the cells, and
    aggregates raw counts by donor and cell type so that the donor,
    not the cell, is the unit of inference (Squair et al. 2021
    <doi:10.1038/s41467-021-25960-2>). The default analysis fits robust
    edgeR quasi-likelihood models with exposure-independent expression
    filtering, complete-transcriptome library sizes, design-rank checks
    and multiplicity correction across all genes and cell types; DESeq2
    and voom-dream backends are also available. Further functions cover
    several exposures at once, donor-level cell-type composition,
    dose-response curves, exposure mixtures, meta-analysis across
    cohorts, power calculation, gene set testing with fgsea and
    imputation below the limit of detection. Exploratory functions
    estimate cross-omic networks within a cell type. All results are
    associations; the package does not identify causal effects.
